# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTROLLED-ACCESS PATIENT DATA — MUST NEVER BE COMMITTED
#
# The challenge data use terms require that the supplied genomic data are not
# redistributed and are deleted within 30 days of the challenge close. This
# working tree is an internal analysis checkout. Publication uses a reviewed
# source snapshot. The organisers permit code, reports, HPO terms and selected
# findings; genome-scale data and reformatted/subset genomic files are excluded.
# See https://huggingface.co/spaces/SageBio/rare-disease-real-kid-mva-hackathon-2026/discussions/2
#
# These rules are deliberately broad and match by extension, not by path, so a
# file placed in an unexpected directory is still caught.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.fastq.*
*.fq
*.fq.gz
*.fq.*
*.bam
*.bam.*
*.bai
*.cram
*.cram.*
*.crai
*.pytor
*.sam
*.sam.gz
*.bcf
*.bcf.*
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf.gz.tbi
*.vcf.*
*.gvcf
*.gvcf.*
*.g.vcf.gz
*.tbi
*.csi
*.docx

# Directories that hold data, references, or tool caches
data/
ref/
vep_cache/
exomiser/
genome_bundle/
work/
.locks/

# Reference/annotation resources (large, redistributable from source instead)
*.fa
*.fa.gz
*.fa.bgz
*.fai
*.gzi
*.dict
*.2bit
*.bwt
*.pac
*.sa
*.amb
*.ann

# Tooling
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
logs_*.txt
*.part
*.lock
*.lockdir

# These exceptions do not certify JSON/CSV as safe. Reviewed publication uses
# an explicit inventory; arbitrary results, logs and derived tables stay local.
!results/*.csv
!results/*.md
!results/*.json
